794
00:30:33,667 --> 00:30:35,368
Is it okay if we just wiggle?

795
00:30:39,105 --> 00:30:40,540
Whoa, jeez.

796
00:30:40,573 --> 00:30:42,942
I thought he was Neil
Diamond for a second there.

797
00:30:45,712 --> 00:30:47,080
(mystical zapping)

798
00:30:47,113 --> 00:30:48,013
Honey, did you use this?

799
00:30:48,047 --> 00:30:49,515
It's all screwed up.

800
00:30:51,050 --> 00:30:53,285
There are still
limits to your strength.

801
00:30:53,318 --> 00:30:54,887
I will find the strength.

802
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:55,888
Could you find the strength

803
00:30:55,922 --> 00:30:58,290
to at least sweep the garage?

804
00:30:59,625 --> 00:31:01,560
Not until you find
the second stone.

805
00:31:01,593 --> 00:31:03,963
Then you can watch cartoons.

806
00:31:05,130 --> 00:31:08,067
The world is
almost in my grasp.

807
00:31:08,100 --> 00:31:10,470
Or at least the Quad Cities.

808
00:31:12,605 --> 00:31:15,140
One man in not
going to stop me.

809
00:31:15,942 --> 00:31:17,677
Young Bill Clinton.

810
00:31:20,078 --> 00:31:22,982
Act natural, pretend
like he's not here.

811
00:31:24,117 --> 00:31:25,518
Okay, okay, Larry
told me what to do

812
00:31:25,552 --> 00:31:27,087
if they try to saddle me.

813
00:31:27,687 --> 00:31:29,855
You and me will
get along just fine.

814
00:31:30,055 --> 00:31:31,257
Bigfoot.

815
00:31:32,892 --> 00:31:33,893
Pretty lucky to
find a wild horse

816
00:31:33,927 --> 00:31:35,695
with a bridle and all.

817
00:31:36,295 --> 00:31:37,197
(horse whinnies)

818
00:31:37,230 --> 00:31:38,998
Okay, good dog, good dog.

819
00:31:39,032 --> 00:31:40,333
Those are my horses.

820
00:31:40,933 --> 00:31:42,302
Get down off him.

821
00:31:42,668 --> 00:31:43,335
Forgive me, I'm--

822
00:31:43,368 --> 00:31:44,137
Unappealing.

823
00:31:44,170 --> 00:31:45,272
Really in a hurry.

824
00:31:45,305 --> 00:31:46,838
(woman whistles)

825
00:31:46,872 --> 00:31:48,240
Puppy, no, no.

826
00:31:48,273 --> 00:31:50,242
(Tom Servo, Mike and Crow cheer)

827
00:31:53,178 --> 00:31:55,848
♪ Shoot that poison
arrow through my heart

828
00:31:55,882 --> 00:31:58,885
No, I told you,
never (murmurs).

829
00:31:58,918 --> 00:32:01,287
Thought you could
outrun an old woman.

830
00:32:01,320 --> 00:32:03,488
Now, come on,
you're 50 years young.

831
00:32:03,522 --> 00:32:05,925
My daughter shoots
pretty good too, doesn't she?

832
00:32:05,958 --> 00:32:07,293
Excellent.

833
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:09,662
Excellent shot.

834
00:32:09,695 --> 00:32:11,763
If there's one thing I've
always admired, it's...

835
00:32:12,865 --> 00:32:13,967
It's--

836
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:16,568
We don't appreciate
horse thieves.

837
00:32:16,602 --> 00:32:19,372
But we appreciate ladies'
night at Blainbrook Bowl.

838
00:32:19,405 --> 00:32:20,673
Horse thieves.

839
00:32:21,140 --> 00:32:23,108
No, a little gold maybe.

840
00:32:23,142 --> 00:32:24,277
A jewel here and there.

841
00:32:24,310 --> 00:32:25,778
- But never a horse.
- Witchiepoo.

842
00:32:25,812 --> 00:32:26,878
Drop your sword.

843
00:32:26,912 --> 00:32:28,547
Like you have your accent.

844
00:32:28,580 --> 00:32:30,450
I'd be more than
happy to pay for him.

845
00:32:30,483 --> 00:32:32,018
Elayne Boosler looks on.

846
00:32:32,052 --> 00:32:33,152
What other
weapons do you have?

847
00:32:33,185 --> 00:32:34,553
Amongst our weaponry are--

848
00:32:34,587 --> 00:32:35,822
A knife?

849
00:32:35,855 --> 00:32:36,922
No knife.

850
00:32:37,890 --> 00:32:39,892
Money's a little
tight at the moment.

851
00:32:39,925 --> 00:32:41,460
But I think we can
work something out.

852
00:32:41,493 --> 00:32:42,762
Search him.

853
00:32:43,328 --> 00:32:45,598
Hi, I'm Cindy, I'll
be searching you.

854
00:32:47,467 --> 00:32:51,437
(Tom Servo hisses)

855
00:32:51,470 --> 00:32:53,940
It's a high school
jousting injury.

856
00:32:57,377 --> 00:32:58,310
No knife.

857
00:32:58,343 --> 00:33:00,245
What's his inseam?

858
00:33:03,215 --> 00:33:04,350
Knife, knife.

859
00:33:04,383 --> 00:33:06,385
I've seen your kind before.

860
00:33:07,387 --> 00:33:08,722
I haven't.

861
00:33:08,755 --> 00:33:11,523
Go ahead, enjoy my area.

862
00:33:11,557 --> 00:33:13,458
Ma'am, have a look.

863
00:33:15,595 --> 00:33:17,463
Okay, if you're done
degrading the human race,

864
00:33:17,497 --> 00:33:19,465
can we get on with the movie?

865
00:33:19,798 --> 00:33:20,733
Don't move.

866
00:33:20,767 --> 00:33:22,102
Mother.

867
00:33:23,302 --> 00:33:25,972
I would not dig
into this guy's pouch.

868
00:33:29,775 --> 00:33:32,245
The anniversary
diamond. (hums a tune)

869
00:33:32,278 --> 00:33:33,780
I thought you
didn't have any money.

870
00:33:33,813 --> 00:33:35,080
This is nothing.

871
00:33:35,113 --> 00:33:36,915
There are thousands more
where this came from.

872
00:33:37,483 --> 00:33:38,852
Tell you what.

873
00:33:39,085 --> 00:33:41,353
You let me borrow a horse,

874
00:33:41,387 --> 00:33:43,555
I'll come back with
a handful of these.

875
00:33:43,890 --> 00:33:45,425
Bigger ones too.

876
00:33:45,458 --> 00:33:46,892
You spend the night here.

877
00:33:46,925 --> 00:33:47,827
Can you reach in my hand?

878
00:33:47,860 --> 00:33:48,928
No, I really am in a hurry.

879
00:33:48,962 --> 00:33:50,228
Oh, you'd kill yourself

880
00:33:50,262 --> 00:33:51,863
trying to ride out of
these canyons in the dark.

881
00:33:51,897 --> 00:33:53,398
It's not dark.

882
00:33:53,432 --> 00:33:56,668
The people who are after
you can't get in very easy.

883
00:33:57,337 --> 00:33:59,038
I'll lend you a
horse in the morning.

884
00:33:59,905 --> 00:34:00,840
Thank you.

885
00:34:00,873 --> 00:34:02,242
Thank you very much.

886
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:04,443
I'm back.

887
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:06,112
You sleep outside.

888
00:34:06,145 --> 00:34:07,947
Everything's outside.

889
00:34:09,015 --> 00:34:13,185
(energetic 80's techno beat)

890
00:34:15,655 --> 00:34:16,755
Man, those are
the biggest peanuts

891
00:34:16,788 --> 00:34:18,323
I've ever seen.

892
00:34:19,825 --> 00:34:21,727
Do you have any Mrs. Dash?

893
00:34:23,528 --> 00:34:25,932
And for dessert,
potato cream pie.

894
00:34:26,498 --> 00:34:28,600
You boil a hell of a potato.

895
00:34:28,633 --> 00:34:30,703
And there'll be
more for breakfast.

896
00:34:30,703 --> 00:34:32,905
(daffy laugh) Daughter smart.

897
00:34:35,708 --> 00:34:38,510
Perhaps in the morning
I can catch you a rabbit.

898
00:34:38,543 --> 00:34:40,045
(wolf howls)

899
00:34:40,112 --> 00:34:42,047
You want to eat a rabbit?

900
00:34:42,115 --> 00:34:43,448
But potatoes are what we eat.

901
00:34:43,515 --> 00:34:45,452
I meant a potato rabbit.

902
00:34:45,652 --> 00:34:47,420
Just a wild idea.

903
00:34:48,822 --> 00:34:50,022
Thank you.

904
00:34:51,223 --> 00:34:53,325
Here's a small hot,
wet pillow for you.

905
00:34:53,358 --> 00:34:55,528
Would you like another potato?

906
00:34:55,562 --> 00:34:57,263
This is the scene
they always show

907
00:34:57,330 --> 00:34:59,132
in That's Entertainment.
(laughs)

908
00:34:59,165 --> 00:35:00,432
Thank you.

909
00:35:01,233 --> 00:35:02,535
You sleep in the barn.

910
00:35:02,568 --> 00:35:03,970
This isn't the barn?

911
00:35:08,140 --> 00:35:09,342
Thank you very much.

912
00:35:09,375 --> 00:35:11,043
The potato sketch,
ladies and gentlemen,

913
00:35:11,043 --> 00:35:12,745
let's hear it for
the potato sketch.

914
00:35:12,745 --> 00:35:15,280
There's only one thing
a man like that wants.

915
00:35:15,347 --> 00:35:16,748
Sour cream with chives.

916
00:35:16,782 --> 00:35:18,150
Careful.

917
00:35:19,552 --> 00:35:20,687
(knocking)

918
00:35:21,687 --> 00:35:22,755
What the?

919
00:35:24,990 --> 00:35:26,992
Hi, we're here to
start on your deck.

920
00:35:27,058 --> 00:35:28,760
What did you do
with my daughter?

921
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:30,930
She's in a cool,
dry place, ma'am.

922
00:35:31,663 --> 00:35:33,332
I'm looking for an outlaw.

923
00:35:33,365 --> 00:35:35,033
Yeah, so am I.

924
00:35:35,835 --> 00:35:37,270
I'll get my purse.

925
00:35:37,870 --> 00:35:39,505
She's an odd duck.

926
00:35:39,538 --> 00:35:42,342
I've got potato
sandwiches for everyone.

927
00:35:45,545 --> 00:35:46,678
No, don't touch me.

928
00:35:46,712 --> 00:35:48,347
It's too icky, ew.

929
00:35:48,882 --> 00:35:50,382
Actif Blue.

930
00:35:51,250 --> 00:35:52,652
We're the knights
of the round table.

931
00:35:52,685 --> 00:35:53,752
Oh.

932
00:35:58,390 --> 00:36:00,192
He knows where the horses are.

933
00:36:00,225 --> 00:36:01,460
(gasps) And to think,

934
00:36:01,493 --> 00:36:03,162
he had earlier
misrepresented his knowledge

935
00:36:03,195 --> 00:36:05,263
of the location of the horses.

936
00:36:06,498 --> 00:36:08,868
Quit chasing me,
I don't like you.

937
00:36:11,270 --> 00:36:13,772
I'll have to ask you to
activate your sonar, ma'am.

938
00:36:15,307 --> 00:36:17,810
He made a saddle
out of Grover.

939
00:36:18,377 --> 00:36:21,947
I did know where the
horses were. (evil laugh)

940
00:36:22,515 --> 00:36:24,417
Horses are what we ride.

941
00:36:26,252 --> 00:36:28,988
Marinda, you
can't come with me.

942
00:36:29,022 --> 00:36:31,257
But you can't get through
these hills without me.

943
00:36:31,290 --> 00:36:34,693
I have to get to my
data entry job anyway.

944
00:36:34,727 --> 00:36:36,262
I've got to try.

945
00:36:36,295 --> 00:36:38,197
But they'll catch you.

946
00:36:38,230 --> 00:36:40,332
I don't want them to catch you.

947
00:36:41,700 --> 00:36:43,668
(Tom Servo, Mike and
Crow grumble in disgust)

948
00:36:43,702 --> 00:36:45,470
He's rubbin' his
entire face against her.

949
00:36:45,503 --> 00:36:47,740
He's gonna swallow
her whole head, ew.

950
00:36:47,773 --> 00:36:49,308
Her nose, ew.

951
00:36:50,743 --> 00:36:53,112
I have to see what it's
like beyond this valley.

952
00:36:53,145 --> 00:36:56,315
Are there Nina B's and
Hurrah Stores out there?

953
00:36:58,952 --> 00:37:01,853
Man, I'm draggin' a
boat anchor with this one.

954
00:37:02,888 --> 00:37:04,290
What are you waiting for?

955
00:37:04,323 --> 00:37:06,858
Waiting 'til I'm
not sharp anymore.

956
00:37:09,262 --> 00:37:11,063
Uh, excuse me,
Mr. Moose Warrior?

957
00:37:11,097 --> 00:37:12,097
I'm a bat.

958
00:37:12,130 --> 00:37:13,865
Squeak, squeak.

959
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:14,800
Squeak.

960
00:37:16,902 --> 00:37:18,770
That's the only way out.

961
00:37:18,803 --> 00:37:21,740
(Tom Servo groans loudly)

962
00:37:24,110 --> 00:37:26,678
Warriors from Hell will
handle it from here, ma'am.

963
00:37:26,712 --> 00:37:28,280
(gasps) Free range potatoes.

964
00:37:28,313 --> 00:37:29,748
I've seen these before.

965
00:37:30,950 --> 00:37:32,985
Pardon us, we weren't
grazing or anything.

966
00:37:36,655 --> 00:37:37,723
Continue to follow me

967
00:37:37,757 --> 00:37:40,292
as you have for days and days.

968
00:37:40,325 --> 00:37:44,497
(Tom Servo imitates
intense music)

969
00:37:46,098 --> 00:37:48,968
Whoa, Dave's horse
is burnin' oil again.

970
00:37:49,735 --> 00:37:51,570
By Prince Matchabelli.

971
00:37:52,237 --> 00:37:53,238
Whoa, that paper mill

972
00:37:53,272 --> 00:37:55,340
is goin' full time these days.

973
00:38:00,478 --> 00:38:03,748
So, beyond my valley,
everything's the same then.

974
00:38:10,355 --> 00:38:11,823
Use tongue as blunt object.

975
00:38:11,857 --> 00:38:13,825
Swab tongue onto every
available surface.

976
00:38:13,858 --> 00:38:15,193
(Mike chuckles)

977
00:38:16,562 --> 00:38:18,630
You're the only
man I ever kissed.

978
00:38:18,663 --> 00:38:20,365
I bagged another
savage chick right here

979
00:38:20,398 --> 00:38:21,900
a couple a years ago.

980
00:38:22,668 --> 00:38:24,137
Take me with you.

981
00:38:24,170 --> 00:38:25,370
I can't.

982
00:38:25,403 --> 00:38:26,738
I'll mail you back
your Foreigner tape.

983
00:38:26,772 --> 00:38:27,973
If you ride out
of these mountains,

984
00:38:28,007 --> 00:38:29,842
you'll leave your
innocence behind.

985
00:38:29,875 --> 00:38:31,243
I believe that's the
first time I ever

986
00:38:31,277 --> 00:38:33,078
told a girl to hang onto her
innocence. (laughs awkwardly)

987
00:38:33,112 --> 00:38:35,715
Ah, that trademark
Relson laugh.

988
00:38:38,850 --> 00:38:39,818
Will you ever come back?

989
00:38:39,852 --> 00:38:40,820
Please say no.

990
00:38:40,853 --> 00:38:41,787
I can't.

991
00:38:43,488 --> 00:38:45,725
You sure you'll
never come back?

992
00:38:47,860 --> 00:38:49,695
You're going now, right?

993
00:38:49,728 --> 00:38:51,163
Goodbye, Steve.

994
00:38:53,265 --> 00:38:56,102
Goodbye, Shelly, hope
your perm works out.

995
00:38:56,135 --> 00:38:58,603
Haven't I seen her
dancing by the pool

996
00:38:58,637 --> 00:39:00,538
with Spuds MacKenzie?

997
00:39:03,642 --> 00:39:05,077
Ah, good.

998
00:39:05,110 --> 00:39:06,978
Always show your audience the
inside of your hero's mouth.

999
00:39:07,012 --> 00:39:09,148
(Mike makes disgusted
vocalizations)

1000
00:39:12,485 --> 00:39:14,853
Oh, it really is the best
part of the human body.

1001
00:39:14,887 --> 00:39:16,588
Mm. (imitates chewing)

1002
00:39:21,493 --> 00:39:23,095
Hey, he was sitting.

1003
00:39:24,130 --> 00:39:26,465
I think she just got
edited to the ground.

1004
00:39:29,535 --> 00:39:30,970
I sprained my dress.

1005
00:39:31,003 --> 00:39:33,405
Damn you, come back.

1006
00:39:34,073 --> 00:39:36,608
Cram it, lady. (goofy laugh)

1007
00:39:37,510 --> 00:39:39,178
This is all your fault.

1008
00:39:39,812 --> 00:39:41,413
Well, well, well.

1009
00:39:41,780 --> 00:39:44,483
If my bodyguards were here,
you wouldn't be smiling.

1010
00:39:45,250 --> 00:39:46,418
Call them then.

1011
00:39:46,452 --> 00:39:47,720
Let me get my
cup back in place.

1012
00:39:47,753 --> 00:39:48,787
There.

1013
00:39:50,655 --> 00:39:51,723
They're dead.

1014
00:39:52,357 --> 00:39:53,692
Those idiot soldiers.

1015
00:39:55,160 --> 00:39:56,762
When they couldn't catch you...

1016
00:39:57,328 --> 00:39:58,663
Hold on, my bra strap.

1017
00:39:58,697 --> 00:40:00,967
They came back and accused
everyone of protecting you.

1018
00:40:01,367 --> 00:40:03,168
Just who exactly
are you anyway?

1019
00:40:03,568 --> 00:40:05,070
That's none of your business.

1020
00:40:06,505 --> 00:40:07,507
You're right.

1021
00:40:07,540 --> 00:40:08,807
Zing.

1022
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:10,742
Wow, it's like Nick
and Nora Charles.

1023
00:40:10,977 --> 00:40:13,745
I better get back to my
Super Weight Gain 2000.

1024
00:40:13,778 --> 00:40:15,380
You're absolutely right.

1025
00:40:16,048 --> 00:40:18,150
I am the Princess Elizena.

1026
00:40:18,183 --> 00:40:19,885
And I can't find my brush.

1027
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:22,353
(Deathstalker chokes and laughs)

1028
00:40:22,688 --> 00:40:25,257
I'm on my way to marry
a very important man.

1029
00:40:25,290 --> 00:40:26,658
Edgar Bronfman.

1030
00:40:26,692 --> 00:40:27,693
Is that so?

1031
00:40:28,227 --> 00:40:30,128
You never even
introduced yourself.

1032
00:40:32,063 --> 00:40:33,232
Forgive me.

1033
00:40:33,265 --> 00:40:34,867
This guy peaked
in the Middle Ages.

1034
00:40:36,835 --> 00:40:38,637
Now they do the
college handshake.

1035
00:40:39,738 --> 00:40:41,640
(smooches) Deathstalker.

1036
00:40:42,107 --> 00:40:43,808
(gasps) From
first hour English?

1037
00:40:43,842 --> 00:40:45,110
You've heard of me, huh?

1038
00:40:45,143 --> 00:40:46,412
(chuckles)

1039
00:40:46,445 --> 00:40:47,780
Don't you touch me.

1040
00:40:47,813 --> 00:40:50,448
(groans) Do I look like
I'm about to hurt anybody?

1041
00:40:50,715 --> 00:40:53,185
I'm just a simple hero
trying to eat his dinner.

1042
00:40:53,218 --> 00:40:55,453
Do you know how
much fat is in that?

1043
00:40:55,855 --> 00:40:56,955
Vole is good tonight.

1044
00:40:56,988 --> 00:40:58,323
Mm. (imitates chewing)

1045
00:40:58,357 --> 00:40:59,725
People talk too
much, you know that?

1046
00:40:59,758 --> 00:41:00,792
They should eat more.

1047
00:41:00,827 --> 00:41:02,460
Just because a man's a little...

1048
00:41:02,495 --> 00:41:03,628
Teapot?

1049
00:41:03,662 --> 00:41:04,897
Faster with a sword.

1050
00:41:04,930 --> 00:41:08,133
A little better with a
horse, a little stronger.

1051
00:41:08,733 --> 00:41:09,968
A little more handsome.

1052
00:41:10,535 --> 00:41:11,903
Brave.

1053
00:41:11,937 --> 00:41:12,838
Daring.

1054
00:41:12,872 --> 00:41:13,938
Odious.

1055
00:41:14,573 --> 00:41:15,207
Hateful.

1056
00:41:15,240 --> 00:41:16,008
Greasy.

1057
00:41:16,042 --> 00:41:16,808
Irresistible to women.

1058
