Look, shut up.

2096
01:22:41,157 --> 01:22:42,192
Sorry.

2097
01:22:45,195 --> 01:22:46,095
Come on, let's roll.

2098
01:22:46,128 --> 01:22:47,530
He doesn't know me.

2099
01:22:49,665 --> 01:22:54,503
(sniffles) Make sure
you crimp the foil good.

2100
01:22:54,970 --> 01:22:57,373
And poke her with a fork
so she doesn't explode.

2101
01:22:57,407 --> 01:22:58,775
(sobs lightly)

2102
01:23:03,012 --> 01:23:05,548
Forget it, Jake,
it's Chinatown.

2103
01:23:06,282 --> 01:23:09,985
That must be ye
forensic pathologist.

2104
01:23:10,587 --> 01:23:12,522
She's gone, you can
stop lookin' there.

2105
01:23:12,555 --> 01:23:13,457
Honey?

2106
01:23:14,190 --> 01:23:15,758
Wow, rigor mortis.

2107
01:23:15,792 --> 01:23:19,095
They must have pounded pieces
of rebar through her body.

2108
01:23:20,497 --> 01:23:21,698
Hey, mister.

2109
01:23:21,732 --> 01:23:23,165
You mind if we throw
our leaves in there?

2110
01:23:27,337 --> 01:23:29,938
The stink, smells
like rotten potatoes.

2111
01:23:31,307 --> 01:23:34,410
This was her
favorite stick. (sobs)

2112
01:23:35,578 --> 01:23:38,448
Boy, that Freeze and
Shine sure goes up fast.

2113
01:23:39,415 --> 01:23:42,185
He's overwhelmed with
feelings of ambiguity.

2114
01:23:43,920 --> 01:23:47,590
Well, I have to say,
she was all righta.

2115
01:23:50,560 --> 01:23:53,463
Let's bring out the
entire cast for a bow.

2116
01:23:55,898 --> 01:23:57,500
Hey, man, anytime
you wanna talk.

2117
01:23:57,533 --> 01:23:59,302
I know you're riding
a major bummer.

2118
01:23:59,335 --> 01:24:01,070
It is you who've earned

2119
01:24:02,072 --> 01:24:04,873
the right to put these together.

2120
01:24:04,907 --> 01:24:07,743
Why is Gabby
Sabatini in back there?

2121
01:24:08,143 --> 01:24:10,045
Oh, and everyone
went in on a card.

2122
01:24:10,080 --> 01:24:11,113
This magic.

2123
01:24:11,147 --> 01:24:12,848
It can't give me what I need.

2124
01:24:12,882 --> 01:24:14,783
We're going back to that
field and jump up and down

2125
01:24:14,817 --> 01:24:16,418
if you want to join us.

2126
01:24:17,353 --> 01:24:19,722
Well, we'll take it
back is you don't want it.

2127
01:24:22,092 --> 01:24:24,327
How does it show where
the city of treasure is?

2128
01:24:24,360 --> 01:24:25,762
It works with a satellite

2129
01:24:25,795 --> 01:24:27,930
that triangulates several
points in the Earth.

2130
01:24:28,230 --> 01:24:32,235
♪ The Wonderful
World of Color

2131
01:24:33,770 --> 01:24:35,272
All my life, my
people have dreamed

2132
01:24:35,305 --> 01:24:37,273
of a kingdom of their own.

2133
01:24:37,307 --> 01:24:38,273
And now, with the stone,

2134
01:24:38,307 --> 01:24:39,842
we can go look for one.

2135
01:24:39,875 --> 01:24:40,910
Now we have one.

2136
01:24:40,943 --> 01:24:41,743
Wait.

2137
01:24:41,778 --> 01:24:45,315
(joyous medieval music)

2138
01:24:45,348 --> 01:24:46,917
Well, by jeweled
cities, they meant dirt

2139
01:24:46,950 --> 01:24:49,318
and horse dung and cheap stucco.

2140
01:24:52,722 --> 01:24:53,857
Stay with me.

2141
01:24:53,890 --> 01:24:56,158
And live in peace
and prosperity?

2142
01:24:56,592 --> 01:24:58,562
Hey, Gandalf,
it's like 98 out.

2143
01:24:58,595 --> 01:25:00,130
Jeez.

2144
01:25:00,163 --> 01:25:02,898
They need a smug bastard
in the next village.

2145
01:25:04,267 --> 01:25:06,368
You told me once it's
not easy being a princess.

2146
01:25:06,402 --> 01:25:07,803
Sure did, goodbye.

2147
01:25:07,837 --> 01:25:09,738
It's not easy
being a hero either.

2148
01:25:10,207 --> 01:25:11,773
Never before has an
entire medieval city

2149
01:25:11,808 --> 01:25:13,810
throw up at the same moment.

2150
01:25:14,277 --> 01:25:16,712
Who knows, maybe there's
another treasure city

2151
01:25:16,745 --> 01:25:18,213
waiting for me out there.

2152
01:25:18,247 --> 01:25:19,648
There isn't.

2153
01:25:20,048 --> 01:25:21,183
Not that you've seen.

2154
01:25:21,217 --> 01:25:22,318
they should find
the first one.

2155
01:25:22,352 --> 01:25:23,452
Who knows.

2156
01:25:25,188 --> 01:25:27,323
You're never
coming back, are you?

2157
01:25:30,125 --> 01:25:34,230
(Crow imitates music)

2158
01:25:37,100 --> 01:25:38,333
(crowd cheers)

2159
01:25:38,367 --> 01:25:41,303
He's leaving, our long
national nightmare is over.

2160
01:25:41,337 --> 01:25:42,538
[Tom Servo and Crow] Yay.

2161
01:25:42,572 --> 01:25:44,907
I wouldn't really
have killed you.

2162
01:25:46,442 --> 01:25:48,978
I find you very attractive.

2163
01:25:49,012 --> 01:25:50,880
Oh, man, I've got
to write Radagast.

2164
01:25:50,913 --> 01:25:52,615
He'll never believe this.

2165
01:25:53,215 --> 01:25:54,650
Don't stop, just keep going.

2166
01:25:54,683 --> 01:25:55,685
No, don't stop.

2167
01:25:55,718 --> 01:25:56,987
Bastard.

2168
01:25:57,920 --> 01:26:01,023
No, this is a door,
that's a blind alley.

2169
01:26:03,660 --> 01:26:05,228
Left a lot of
things unresolved.

2170
01:26:05,262 --> 01:26:06,795
There's some loose
ends back there.

2171
01:26:06,828 --> 01:26:08,898
Yeah, the girl didn't
roast all the way.

2172
01:26:08,932 --> 01:26:10,833
What should we do with her?

2173
01:26:11,433 --> 01:26:14,870
♪ Chisum, John Chisum

2174
01:26:16,405 --> 01:26:20,810
(Tom Servo imitates music)

2175
01:26:21,343 --> 01:26:25,282
(speaks in gibberish)

2176
01:26:27,583 --> 01:26:30,118
Music by a total spaz.

2177
01:26:32,455 --> 01:26:34,923
Dead warriors as themselves.

2178
01:26:41,163 --> 01:26:42,498
There really wasn't
any death stalking

2179
01:26:42,532 --> 01:26:44,167
in this film, was there?

2180
01:26:44,200 --> 01:26:46,802
Gettin' all Keith
Emerson-y on us now.

2181
01:26:46,835 --> 01:26:48,705
Emerson-y.
Emerson-y.

2182
01:26:48,738 --> 01:26:50,138
It's hard to say.

2183
01:26:52,242 --> 01:26:56,212
(all imitate music)

2184
01:26:56,245 --> 01:26:57,513
Uh, Mr. Relson?

2185
01:26:57,547 --> 01:27:00,950
The shot's done, you can
come back, Mr. Relson.

2186
01:27:02,218 --> 01:27:03,085
Everybody.

2187
01:27:03,118 --> 01:27:07,190
(all imitate music)

2188
01:27:12,195 --> 01:27:13,730
♪ You can dance if you want to

2189
01:27:13,763 --> 01:27:16,332
♪ You can leave
your friends behind

2190
01:27:16,365 --> 01:27:18,133
♪ 'Cause your friends don't

2191
01:27:18,167 --> 01:27:19,602
All the underpaid Mexicans.

2192
01:27:19,635 --> 01:27:22,172
Yes, your NAFTA
dollars at work.

2193
01:27:23,807 --> 01:27:25,842
This doesn't get
annoying at all, does it?

2194
01:27:25,875 --> 01:27:28,477
Isn't this side two
of Terrapin Station?

2195
01:27:32,015 --> 01:27:34,017
I'd like to shoot
everybody in this movie,

2196
01:27:34,050 --> 01:27:35,585
entirely in Mexico.

2197
01:27:35,618 --> 01:27:39,422
(all imitate music)

2198
01:27:42,492 --> 01:27:46,928
(mechanical blips and whirs)
(bubbling)

2199
01:27:52,135 --> 01:27:53,402
Hey.

2200
01:27:53,435 --> 01:27:55,605
Hey, Servo, you gonna help
us out with this letter?

2201
01:27:55,638 --> 01:27:56,805
In a minute, Miker.

2202
01:27:56,838 --> 01:27:58,140
Almost done here.
(metallic clanging)

2203
01:27:58,173 --> 01:27:59,142
Okay, alright.

2204
01:27:59,175 --> 01:28:01,143
Well, we have a letter here from

2205
01:28:01,177 --> 01:28:02,878
Shane MacGowan of the Popes.

2206
01:28:02,912 --> 01:28:03,780
Hi, Shane.

2207
01:28:03,813 --> 01:28:05,315
No, Mallory MacGowan.

2208
01:28:05,348 --> 01:28:06,282
I'm kidding.

2209
01:28:06,315 --> 01:28:07,583
He wouldn't write a letter.

2210
01:28:07,617 --> 01:28:10,620
Dear Mystery Science
Theater 3000, how are you?

2211
01:28:11,187 --> 01:28:11,720
Fine.

2212
01:28:11,753 --> 01:28:12,788
I'm fine.

2213
01:28:12,822 --> 01:28:13,923
I'm almost 10.

2214
01:28:13,957 --> 01:28:15,858
Can I have everyone's
photograph?

2215
01:28:16,358 --> 01:28:18,995
I think, you know, if
she's 10, she's old enough.

2216
01:28:19,028 --> 01:28:20,363
I watch your show every weekend.

2217
01:28:20,397 --> 01:28:21,930
Will you please write back?

2218
01:28:21,963 --> 01:28:22,965
You do that.

2219
01:28:22,998 --> 01:28:24,167
I'm right on it.

2220
01:28:24,200 --> 01:28:25,335
I have one brother
and one sister.

2221
01:28:25,368 --> 01:28:26,502
I live in Morro Bay.

2222
01:28:26,535 --> 01:28:28,003
Well, got to go.

2223
01:28:28,037 --> 01:28:29,338
It was getting a little long.

2224
01:28:29,372 --> 01:28:30,607
So, thank you, Mallory.

2225
01:28:30,640 --> 01:28:31,973
That's a nice letter there.

2226
01:28:32,008 --> 01:28:33,308
Whew, boy, let me tell ya.

2227
01:28:33,342 --> 01:28:34,810
There you go Mike.

2228
01:28:34,843 --> 01:28:36,512
Got a wild hare and forged
us up a ring of power.

2229
01:28:36,545 --> 01:28:38,347
You know, one ring
to rule us all.

2230
01:28:38,380 --> 01:28:40,048
One to find us.

2231
01:28:40,082 --> 01:28:42,218
One ring to bring us all,
and in the darkness...

2232
01:28:43,118 --> 01:28:43,920
Bind us.
Bind us.

2233
01:28:43,953 --> 01:28:45,220
Yes, very good.

2234
01:28:45,253 --> 01:28:46,222
Why don't ya slip that
on, see what happens.

2235
01:28:46,255 --> 01:28:47,490
Oh, sure, okay.

2236
01:28:47,523 --> 01:28:48,423
(Crow and Tom Servo gasp)

2237
01:28:48,457 --> 01:28:49,458
There we go.

2238
01:28:51,527 --> 01:28:52,295
No.

2239
01:28:52,328 --> 01:28:52,995
Nothin', huh?

2240
01:28:53,028 --> 01:28:54,130
Nobody feels bound?

2241
01:28:54,163 --> 01:28:55,465
Well, you know what,

2242
01:28:55,498 --> 01:28:57,267
I'll bet the fire
wasn't just hot enough.

2243
01:28:57,300 --> 01:28:58,300
Why don't you give
me back that ring,

2244
01:28:58,333 --> 01:28:59,868
and I'll zap around
for another minute.

2245
01:28:59,902 --> 01:29:01,103
Sure.

2246
01:29:01,137 --> 01:29:02,105
Put it in the old
forge, see what happens.

2247
01:29:02,138 --> 01:29:03,205
Okay, be careful now.

2248
01:29:03,238 --> 01:29:04,107
I'll be right back.

2249
01:29:04,140 --> 01:29:04,807
Okay.

2250
01:29:04,840 --> 01:29:06,242
We'll be right here.

2251
01:29:06,275 --> 01:29:07,243
Whoa. (yells)

2252
01:29:07,277 --> 01:29:10,480
Why hast thou summoned
me from Caza Doom?

2253
01:29:10,513 --> 01:29:11,680
Speak.

2254
01:29:11,713 --> 01:29:13,048
(laughs nervously) It's okay.

2255
01:29:13,082 --> 01:29:13,950
It's all under control.

2256
01:29:13,983 --> 01:29:15,183
Fire is just a little hot.

2257
01:29:15,217 --> 01:29:17,187
There, there, there.

2258
01:29:18,755 --> 01:29:19,922
There, that oughta do it.

2259
01:29:19,955 --> 01:29:21,223
Why don't ya try that on, Mike.

2260
01:29:21,257 --> 01:29:22,158
Uh, sure.

2261
01:29:22,192 --> 01:29:23,325
Careful, it's a little hot.

2262
01:29:23,358 --> 01:29:24,160
Oh, it's fine.

2263
01:29:24,193 --> 01:29:25,027
Okay.

2264
01:29:26,462 --> 01:29:28,097
Yeah, I think that's got it.

2265
01:29:28,130 --> 01:29:29,932
Feels like it's bringing us all,

2266
01:29:29,965 --> 01:29:31,733
and in the darkness, you know.

2267
01:29:31,767 --> 01:29:32,368
Binding us.

2268
01:29:32,402 --> 01:29:33,635
Great, great.

2269
01:29:33,668 --> 01:29:34,570
Just don't wear it
around any nazgul.

2270
01:29:34,603 --> 01:29:36,038
But you probably know that.

2271
01:29:36,072 --> 01:29:37,573
And if you have any
questions, I'll be over here,

2272
01:29:37,607 --> 01:29:39,408
forgin' up those seven
rings for the dwarf lords

2273
01:29:39,442 --> 01:29:40,810
and their halls of stone.

2274
01:29:40,843 --> 01:29:41,910
Right-o.

2275
01:29:41,943 --> 01:29:43,578
(dramatic moaning)

2276
01:29:43,612 --> 01:29:48,417
Clayton.

2277
01:29:49,718 --> 01:29:52,988
Clayton, Clayton.

2278
01:29:53,255 --> 01:29:55,190
Clayton.

2279
01:29:55,223 --> 01:29:57,993
Clayton, Clayton.

2280
01:29:58,427 --> 01:29:59,762
Clayton.

2281
01:30:00,597 --> 01:30:03,632
Clayton, Clayton.

2282
01:30:04,300 --> 01:30:05,333
Clayton.

2283
01:30:05,635 --> 01:30:06,768
Clayton.

2284
01:30:07,203 --> 01:30:08,170
Clayton?

2285
01:30:08,603 --> 01:30:09,705
Clayton?

2286
01:30:10,172 --> 01:30:13,175
Clayton, Clayton.

2287
01:30:14,610 --> 01:30:15,445
Clayton?

2288
01:30:16,778 --> 01:30:21,317
(sweeping trumpet music)

2289
01:31:19,175 --> 01:31:21,377
But potatoes are what we eat.
